# ─── Private working area ─────────────────────────────────────
# Everything under _internal/ stays local, with NO exceptions — not even a
# README. An earlier version whitelisted _internal/README.md so the convention
# would be self-documenting in the repo; that was a mistake, because the README
# itself had to describe what it was excluding in order to be useful, and that
# description was the disclosure. The convention is documented in
# CONTRIBUTING-style prose elsewhere instead; the folder is simply opaque.
_internal/

# Machine-specific setup and environment records: hostname, local paths,
# toolchain state. Useful to keep, never to publish.
SETUP_LOG.md
env_day*.txt
env/
